# SPF passes only for the provider's domain and nothing is signed: DMARC fails and the policy says reject.
client-ip: 192.0.2.3
helo: mail.example.com
mail-from: bounce@esp.example.net
authserv-id: mx.receiver.example
[zone]
esp.example.net TXT v=spf1 ip4:192.0.2.3 -all
_dmarc.example.com TXT v=DMARC1; p=reject
[message]
From: Alice <alice@example.com>
To: Bob <bob@receiver.example>
Subject: Fixture
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Message-ID: <fx1@example.com>

Hello Bob.
[expect]
mx.receiver.example; spf=pass smtp.mailfrom=bounce@esp.example.net; dkim=none; dmarc=fail (p=REJECT sp=REJECT dis=REJECT) header.from=example.com
